Use this HTML inside your table column. The CSS draws an **amber warning triangle with an exclamation mark**.

```html
<td>
    <span class="posting-restriction-icon"
          title="Customer has a posting restriction"
          role="img"
          aria-label="Customer has a posting restriction"></span>
</td>
```

```css
.posting-restriction-icon {
    position: relative;
    display: inline-block;
    width: 24px;
    height: 22px;
    vertical-align: middle;
    cursor: help;
}

.posting-restriction-icon::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 0;
    height: 0;
    border-left: 12px solid transparent;
    border-right: 12px solid transparent;
    border-bottom: 22px solid #f5b301;
}

.posting-restriction-icon::after {
    content: "!";
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 1px;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    text-align: center;
    font: bold 15px/16px Arial, sans-serif;
    color: #513600;
}
```

Render the `<span>` only when the customer has a posting restriction. Hovering over it shows the tooltip.

